Q8 vendor-gemm-survey tooling, developed before the AOCL/LPGEMM build window:

* scripts/vendor/build_aocl_lpgemm_zen4.sh - build AOCL-BLIS 5.3.2 LPGEMM from
  source with an explicit Zen4 configuration (classic ./configure path: the
  CMake project() requires Fortran, which this host does not have) and emit a
  full reproducibility report (commit, commands, durations, artifact sha256,
  symbol and generated-header evidence).
* scripts/vendor/run_heavy_with_retry.sh - detached local-lock waiter that
  retries run_local_heavy.sh on rc 75/69 instead of busy-spinning.
* scripts/vendor/q8_perf_matrix_heavy.sh - one heavy window: semantics probe,
  parity probe, then the four-way GEMM matrix.
* scripts/perf/aocl_semantics_probe.py - E1-E9 ctypes experiment set
  (minimal runnable case, accum width, int32 overflow, reserved code, SCALE
  post-op granularity, bf16 RNE tie case, sym_quant single/multi-group,
  runtime arch, exported symbols).
* scripts/perf/w8a8_vendor_parity_probe.py - bit-level parity matrix over
  K tails, sign patterns, the K bound and the overflow case.
* scripts/perf/vendor_gemm_matrix.py - W8J-comparable 12-shape matrix:
  oneDNN (vLLM CPU path) vs AOCL/LPGEMM (packed/unpacked, fused sym_quant)
  vs libxsmm (reported unavailable-with-reason) vs our AVX-512 bf16 bridge and
  native W8A8 kernels, with per-shape bitwise checks.
* scripts/perf/preflight_ours_w8a8.py - compiles one small AVX-512 artifact
  and verifies our kernel is bitwise with the portable golden and fail-closed
  on the reserved -128 code point.
* scripts/perf/summarize_matrix.py - turns the raw matrix JSON into the brief's
  markdown tables.
* docs/pypto_x/0001-2026-09-11-gemm-provider-contract.zh-CN.md - provider
  metadata fields, fail-closed rules and precision_class reporting draft.
