+"""Q8 / vendor-gemm-survey: four-way GEMM matrix on the W8J 12-shape set.
+
+Columns:
+
+  onednn_bf16          vLLM CPU ``dispatch_cpu_unquantized_gemm`` -> oneDNN
+                       (bf16 only: this environment has no standalone oneDNN
+                       and no int8 GEMM API reachable through torch)
+  aocl_int8_*          AOCL-BLIS 5.3.2 LPGEMM s8xs8->s32 (int32 accumulator,
+                       the contract-exact path), B pre-reordered or runtime-packed
+  aocl_int8_symquant   the same GEMM fused with the single-group sym_quant
+                       epilogue (per-row A scale x per-column B scale -> bf16)
+  aocl_bf16_*          AOCL bf16 GEMM (f32 accumulation) -> bf16
+  ours_int8_qmatmul    PyPTO-X native AVX-512 VNNI s8xs8->s32 kernel
+  ours_int8_epilogue   PyPTO-X native single-rounding int32 -> bf16 epilogue
+  ours_bf16            the W8J packed AVX-512 bf16 bridge
+  libxsmm_*            only when a usable build is present (this host: none)
+
+Methodology is copied from the W8J J2 shape gate so the numbers are
+comparable: the same 12 (m,k,n) rows, deterministic inputs
+``randn/sqrt(k) -> bf16`` with the same generator seed, affinity pinned to
+``--threads`` CPUs, the same ``rounds`` timed rounds of ``iters`` calls with
+one warm call per round, median headline plus raw rounds.
+
+Every column is checked against the portable contract baseline in the same
+run: int8 columns must reproduce the portable int32 accumulator bit-for-bit,
+the fused sym_quant column must reproduce the portable bf16 epilogue bits
+(or the mismatch is counted), and bf16 columns are compared with F.linear.
+
+UNGATED: 12 vCPU KVM, no cpufreq control, non-quiet window.
